  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Hurricane Melissa 2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Hurricane Melissa has made landfall in southwestern Jamaica as a Category 5 storm on 28 October, one of the strongest to hit the island nation in modern history. With winds of nearly 300km (185 miles) per hour, Hurricane Melissa is the most powerful tropical storm recorded this year globally. Catastrophic winds with total structural failure are expected near the path of the center of Melissa, in addition to catastrophic flash flooding, landslides, and destructive winds across the rest of the island.&#xa0;In&#xa0;Haiti&#xa0;and the&#xa0;Dominican Republic, heavy rainfall and flooding have caused fatalities and structural damage even before the storm&#x2019;s core has arrived.&#xa0;Cuba&#xa0;has placed multiple southern provinces on alert, and officials in the&#xa0;Bahamas&#xa0;and&#xa0;Turks and Caicos are preparing for possible severe impacts later in the week.</narrative>
  </description>
